On Sun, 2014-05-11 at 04:35 -0700, Mahbubeh Parsaeian wrote:
> Hi INLA team
>
> I want to run a Besag model at country level in the Word shape file. I
> have 101 islands in my data set and when I run the model the warning
> about” 106 connected components” appears. I have searched about this
> problem and understood that the graph consists of 106 disconnected sub
> graphs and I should change the adjust.for.con.comp = FALSE where TRUE
> is default. My problem is that when I change this argument, the
> predicted values are approximately equal to the observed data, I mean
> the correlation between the predicted values and observed data are
> about 1. I run a simple regression model to see how the results are
> different from simple regression. The result is as follows.

Hi,

there is an implicite assumption in the besag-model that the graph is
connected and the question is what to do when its not. the default
behaviour is to use a hierarchical model with one besag-model for each
connected component but with a common precision parameter. if you set
adjust.for.con.comp=FALSE, then no corrections is made (except the rank
deficiancy), but this might lead to an improper posterior.

if you want, I can have a look at the results if you send me the graph
and data and how to run it, so I can provide some more insight.

Best
H

--
