Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi All,

I want to make a sigmodial regression (i.e., a logistic without the 0 to 1 limit) in INLA with a negative binomial or quasipoisson distribution, as the one specified below in BUGS language. I don't know how to specify such a model, if possible, in the formula required by INLA.

Any help would be much appreciated.

Ignacio

# Sigmodal regression y ~ b_0 / (1 + exp(b_1 + b_2*x[i]))

model {

  # priors

  b_0 ~ dnorm(0, 0.001)

  b_1 ~ dnorm(0, 0.001)

  b_2 ~ dnorm(0, 0.001)

  alpha <- exp(lalpha)

  lalpha ~ dnorm(0,0001)

  # likelihood

  for (i in 1:N.po) {

    y[i] ~ dpois(must[i])

    must[i] <- rho[i] * lambda[i]

    rho[i] ~ dgamma(alpha, alpha)

    log(lambda[i]) <- b_0 / (1 + exp(z[i]))

    z[i] <- b_1 + b_2*x[i]

  }

}

