Dear INLA team,

I am working on the implementation of a model with nonlinear interactions in INLA such as:

formula= z~f(x, y, model="rw2")

When I plot the effects, I visualize an overall non-linear possitive slope. This is the exact opposite to what I would expect based on my exploratory analysis and the nature of the phenomenon. More confusingly the trend is the opposite to what I obtain when I run a linear interaction either as:

formula=x*y

or as
w= x*y
formula= z~ w

in which case I obtain a negative slope for the interacting term.

I would deeply appreciate any feedback to understand this outcome as I haven't been able to find any useful information to help me overcome this situation.

