I've been working with models where a higher number would be needed (e.g. dx.doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.12180 <http://dx.doi.org/10.1111/2041-210X.12180>), but I agree that the number of hyperparameters is going to be the problem - I assume the computational costs get huge. I don't know if it's practicable to generalise the function to iidXd and let the user worry if X is so large their computation becomes a major contributor to global warming. So, in practice an extension to 7d, and beyond, would be attractive, but I don't know how much effort it would take.

Bob

